	(text "Fault lines are open drain with pull-ups at the source; EIRQ on falling edge.\nNTC_SW2/3 on ADC2_P3/P4. SW_LHI (PTE4) output, driven low; never asserted in normal operation."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 541.02 248.92 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "7828a0ac-b414-53f9-9878-8f18255e9c2d")
	)
	(text "One 33R at U401 on every SPI line the MCU drives toward an output switch (SCK, MOSI, CS_L), and on the log\nflash's SCK. TI's TPS2HCS08-Q1 data sheet (SLVSHR0, Figure 9-1 and Table 9-1) draws RSPI on all four lines:\n22R typical, optional, for EMI and transient limits; its SPI timing (6.6) is given with 220R. 33R is the board's\nseries value (R503/R504). The switch's SDO has its resistor at the switch (R608/R708/R808, pages 6 to 8).\n<NET>_MCU is the stub from the ball to the resistor; <NET> keeps the line, its test point and its sheet pin.\nPlace each resistor at its ball. Decisions S01 to S03, placement/2026-11-13-spi-series-r."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 434.34 424.18 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "86cf5b0d-0f7a-50ac-8d09-72c72670e763")
	)
